# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values.
# `.env` is gitignored and must never be committed or synced to Drive. chmod 600.
#
# =============================================================================
# Where keys live
# =============================================================================
# INHERITABLE   ~/.config/secrets/*.env (mode 600, dir 700) holds only keys that
#               are genuinely usable across many projects — a personal API key,
#               the MIT Parley key. ~/.zshrc exports them into every interactive
#               shell, so anything reading them from the environment finds them.
#
# PROJECT       this file. The normal case: one labelled key per provider,
#               named for the account that issued it.
#
# =============================================================================
# Naming: label the key after where it came from
# =============================================================================
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_JPAL1='sk-ant-...'     # J-PAL org key #1
# OPENAI_API_KEY_ORG_1234='sk-...'         # label = <ORG><identifier>
#
# The label is documentation that stays with the key, so when an org reissues
# credentials you can tell which project holds which key.
#
# =============================================================================
# The catch: SDKs only read ONE name
# =============================================================================
# The Anthropic SDK reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and nothing else; a labelled key is
# invisible to it. So bind label -> canonical at startup:
#
#     from env_keys import load_keys
#     load_keys()          # call once, before constructing any client
#
# Resolution order per provider, first match wins:
#   1. canonical name set explicitly below            (escape hatch)
#   2. exactly one CANONICAL_<LABEL> below            (the normal case)
#   3. CANONICAL_ACTIVE=<LABEL> picks one of several
#   4. inherited from the environment                 (secrets dir, or CI secrets)
#
# Two or more labelled keys with no _ACTIVE selector raises an error rather than
# guessing — the wrong key bills the wrong account and fails far from the cause.
#
# Requires python-dotenv. Verify wiring with:  python code/test_env_keys.py
#
# =============================================================================
# Conventions
# =============================================================================
# - Quote as KEY='value'. Single quotes are literal in both python-dotenv and
#   shell `source`, so a backslash or $ in a value survives intact.
# - No `export` prefix here (it belongs in ~/.config/secrets/*.env, which the
#   shell sources). python-dotenv strips it, but stricter parsers do not.
# - Never set keys with `launchctl setenv` — it does not survive a reboot and
#   only reaches processes launchd starts afterward, so it produces keys that
#   work intermittently and silently shadow newer ones.
# =============================================================================

# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_JPAL1='sk-ant-api03-REPLACE_ME'
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_ACTIVE=JPAL1        # only needed if several labelled keys exist

# Other project-specific variables (no inheritable tier — set them here).
# DATABASE_URL=
# OAUTH_TOKEN=
